MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=12
DESCRIPTION=KeyQuorum pin, ABI and first consumers. third_party/keyquorum moves from 8ab454b (ABI 3) to KeyQuorum merged main 1fa6aab, the merge commit of KeyQuorum pull request #187 (ABI 5), which carries the merged KeyQuorum #180 work (the store-free kind-17 snapshot open and the kq_file_seal_snapshot, kq_file_open_snapshot and kq_file_snapshot_covers exports, kq_slot_open, kq_bridge_prove, kq_bridge_verify, kq_bridge_connects, kq_access_requirement, KQER error reports) and kq_file_head_author. FL_KQ_ABI_VERSION in contracts/drivers/contract_p4_keyquorum.h is 5, so the driver probe (kq_probe) still requires equality with the linked archive, and docs/FILE_SHARING_KEYQUORUM.md states the ABI 5 probe. test_kq_net gains test_a_refused_ack_is_recorded_as_refused_over_the_wire: a refused ACK is recorded as refused, never as delivered. Consumers: the driver gains a head_author op over kq_file_head_author, fl_kq_cp_head_author names a tracked file's single head author, and fl_kq_autosign_head_author is the autosign job's callback, so a forked file is audited as kq-autosign-forked and not signed (no production caller registers autosign jobs yet). A refused receive signs a KQER report as the online account and writes it as a .kqer sidecar in the landing directory (fl_kq_report_refusal; nothing is written and kq-report-offline is audited when no account is online), and fl_kq_cp_inject_report_with verifies a held report and appends one ErrorReported event to the file's history; the session wire does not carry the sidecar to the sender yet. The other consumers (FL-04, FL-12, FL-14, FL-15) follow.
